INT. SUBMARINE USS HALCYON - CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

Red battle lamps. Pipes sweating. Dials and valves everywhere. The hull creaks like an old ship's timbers.

CAPTAIN DOMINIC ARCHER-LYLE, fifties, hands clasped behind his back, stands before the periscope well. LIEUTENANT PATRICIA "PAT" NOLAN, thirties, executive officer, checks a depth gauge. From a speaker in the bulkhead, the voice of the sonar operator, unseen.

ARCHER-LYLE
(to the room)
Gentlemen, we hold at two hundred feet. Silent running.

NOLAN
Aye, sir.

ARCHER-LYLE
Mr. Nolan, report.

NOLAN
All systems nominal, Captain. Battery at seventy percent.

ARCHER-LYLE
(muttering)
Seventy. Enough for a day.

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Control, sonar. Surface contact, bearing one-two-zero. Single screw. Slow.

ARCHER-LYLE
Merchant?

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
Can't say, sir. No transponder.

ARCHER-LYLE
Pat, plot it.

NOLAN
Plotting.

She bends over a chart table. A ruler, a pencil, a quiet scratch. The sub rocks gently.

ARCHER-LYLE
(low)
Quiet night.

NOLAN
Too quiet, sir?

ARCHER-LYLE
Never say that on my boat.

She smiles. A drip falls from a pipe onto the chart. She wipes it.

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Control, contact is stationary. Engines idle.

ARCHER-LYLE
Odd.

NOLAN
Waiting for us?

ARCHER-LYLE
Or for someone else.

Silence. The lamps pulse. Nolan straightens.

NOLAN
Captain, request permission to raise the scope.

ARCHER-LYLE
Granted. Slowly.

She turns the wheel. The periscope hums up. She folds the handles and puts her eye to it. Her face tightens.

ARCHER-LYLE (CONT'D)
Well?

NOLAN
It's a hospital ship, sir.

ARCHER-LYLE
A hospital ship.

NOLAN
White hull. Red crosses. All lit up.

ARCHER-LYLE
(to himself)
Of course.

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Control, sonar. New contact. Fast. Bearing zero-nine-five. Closing.

NOLAN
Captain!

ARCHER-LYLE
Range?

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
Two thousand yards.

ARCHER-LYLE
Is it hostile?

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
It's ours, sir. Destroyer.

NOLAN
Then why is it running dark?

ARCHER-LYLE
(very quietly)
Because it's escorting.

NOLAN
Escorting what?

ARCHER-LYLE
The hospital ship, Pat. Which means--

AUGUSTO (V.O.)
(over intercom, sharp)
Torpedo in the water! Bearing one-eight-zero! Not ours!

ARCHER-LYLE
(to the room)
Dive! Dive! Rig for impact!

Klaxons. Red lamps flash. The deck tilts. Nolan grabs a rail.

NOLAN
Captain, they're targeting the ship!

ARCHER-LYLE
Then we are the only thing in the way.

NOLAN
Sir?

ARCHER-LYLE
Come to heading one-eight-zero. Full ahead.

NOLAN
Sir, that's suicide!

ARCHER-LYLE
That is the job.

She stares at him. He stares back. She breathes in once.

NOLAN
Aye aye, sir.

She spins the wheel. The engines roar. The sub heels hard. In the periscope's last frame, a white hull glides unknowing through the dark, and between it and the death streaking toward it, a long grey shape cuts across.
